{
  "id": "Compound::DB00663 - Gene::866",
  "verbalization": "Flumethasone Pivalate, through its structural resemblance to other glucocorticoids, is linked to Serpina6 via a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Flumethasone Pivalate, as a glucocorticoid, binds to Serpina6, which is a component of the serpin protease inhibitor family. This relationship is supported by the shared structural similarities with Fluocortolone and Halobetasol Propionate, both of which are known to interact with Serpina6. The lowest common ancestors in the paths highlight the broader classification of these compounds as therapeutic glucocorticoids and hydroxy steroids, reinforcing their common pharmacological profile. The integration of these pathways underscores the role of Serpina6 in mediating the effects of glucocorticoids, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Flumethasone Pivalate influences cellular processes through interactions with this protease inhibitor.",
